      "side": 1,
      "message": "why not just give this an unbounded LinkedBlockingQueue? The rejected execution handler seems rather aggressive. If an app queues up 40 things in a burst they will have gone from that work being drained by a dozen threads to 20 of those being split over 20 threads, 20 of them drained by a single thread, and their thread that queued up the work constantly preempted by a Thread.sleep().\n\nEven if that\u0027s a rare use it seems too opinionated for such a generic utility.",
